text.section:
It is unlawful for a manufacturer or guarantor of commercial feed to:

Manufacture or distribute any commercial feed that is adulterated or misbranded;


Adulterate or misbrand any commercial feed;


Remove or dispose of a commercial feed in violation of an order issued pursuant to § 3.2-4813;


Fail to obtain a license in accordance with § 3.2-4803;


Fail to register medicated feed, small package commercial feed, or specialty pet food in accordance with § 3.2-4804;


Obstruct or hinder the Commissioner in the performance of his duties under this chapter or otherwise attempt to prevent the Commissioner from performing these duties; or


Use metal of any kind, including any hook, snap, staple, or other fastener or device, to secure a package or attach any card, label, or ticket to a package containing feed.
